{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/427301-how-does-promethean-interact-with-the-restless-dead","id":427301,"title":"How does Promethean interact with the Restless Dead?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T20:30:15-08:00","id":427301,"title":"How does Promethean interact with the Restless Dead?","content":"I do not own the game yet. Pick up $20 to $50 a month in stuff, but haven't got this one yet. I need to know which of the Created (Type and Faction) would be most likely to deal with ghosts, as friend and foe. Or do they simply bypass the dead altogether?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:38:37-08:00","id":427323,"title":"","content":"The Ulgan Lineage is the \u201cwe deal with ephemeral entities\u201d Lineage. By default, they deal with spirits; but at least in 1e, they were also the go-to Lineage for dealing with ghosts. <br /> <br /> The Argentum Refinement is dedicated to studying non-Promethean supernatural phenomena, and a follower of this Refinement can <i>easily</i> choose to specialize in all things post-death, such as ghosts, vampires, and zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T13:36:02-08:00","id":429226,"title":"","content":"Osirans have their choice of being able to repeatedly return from the dead or to talk to corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:05:54-07:00","id":439629,"title":"","content":"I believe that Prometheans would have varied reactions to Ghosts and the beings of the Underworld. <br /> <br /> On one hand the Created can learn a great deal about being human by studying Ghosts and the Anchors that keep these departed humans bound to the lands of the living. Perhaps a Milestone could be hidden in witnessing a Ghost being put to rest by having their final desires fullfilled.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Ghosts tend to be highly volatile entities at the best of times and are particularly prone to anger when their Haunt or remains are disturbed. This just creates another danger for the Promethean on top of all of the other dangers that being one of the Created entails. Not to mention that Ghosts primarily interact with the world in their ephemeral form and thus are relatively safe from most Prometheans while hidden in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:09:20-07:00","id":464161,"title":"","content":"Thank you all. Getting more stuff figured out slowly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:27:08-07:00","id":464183,"title":"","content":"There's also the raven athanor for ulgans, which allows the ulgan to spend reagent to find the nearest haunted location or ghost, or give essence to a ghost, and when redeemed gain unseen sense- ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}